# Proposed repair — Item `host`, AC-1 when step "halve twice"

## Decision

Widen the existing `when` concept **`halve`**. Its Public interface item (the Halve control) and kind of use (pressing it to halve the entered number) already exist, so no new concept is added and the Story is left untouched. The current means fixes the use at exactly one halving; the widened means states, in closed prose, every variation the concept admits — one halving or two — matching the product description's bound that three or more presses are not supported.

**Owner of this change:** Product Owner (concept means).

## Exact change — `docs/product/product.yaml`

One field changes: `concepts.when[0].means` of the concept `halve`.

### Before

```json
    "when": [
      {
        "concept": "halve",
        "means": "Halve the entered number once.",
        "terms": []
      }
    ],
```

### After

```json
    "when": [
      {
        "concept": "halve",
        "means": "Halve the entered number, either once or twice in succession; halving it more than twice is not admitted.",
        "terms": []
      }
    ],
```

